<GuideLayout 
  title="The B2B Manufacturing Timeline: From Design to Delivery" 
  type="TIMELINE"
  description="Manage your expectations. A detailed breakdown of the time required for sampling, mass production, and global shipping."
>
  <h2>Planning Your Collection Launch</h2>
  <p>Plan sample development, sample approval, bulk production, dispatch and international transit as separate stages. The final door-to-door schedule depends on revisions, materials and the confirmed logistics route.</p>
  
  <h3>Phase 1: Development & Sampling</h3>
  <p>{businessFacts.oem.sampleDevelopment} Tech-pack finalization, sourcing and revisions may add time.</p>

  <h3>Phase 2: Mass Production</h3>
  <p>{businessFacts.oem.bulkProduction} This includes applicable material preparation, cutting, sewing and quality checks.</p>

  <h3>Phase 3: Quality Control & Packing</h3>
  <p>Every piece is inspected, trimmed, ironed, and packed into your custom branded packaging.</p>

  <h3>Phase 4: Dispatch and International Transit</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>{businessFacts.readyStock.dispatch}</li>
    <li>{businessFacts.shipping}</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Pro Tip: Peak Seasons</h3>
  <p>Always add 2-3 weeks to your timeline if you are producing around major holidays like Chinese New Year or the October National Day, as logistics networks often become congested.</p>
</GuideLayout>
